      "description": "Watch New York City FC vs Chicago Fire highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. The MLS season delivered another classic on July 26, 2026 , as New York City FC and Chicago Fire FC engaged in a high-stakes battle for dominance. From the first whistle, it was clear that both sides were committed to an attacking philosophy, turning the pitch into a theater of tactical maneuvers and clinical finishing. A First-Half Goal Fest Chicago Fire FC started with predatory intent, catching the home side off guard in the opening exchanges. Nicolas Fernandez broke the deadlock in the 10th minute with a strike that stunned the local supporters. The momentum stayed firmly with the visitors as Joel Waterman doubled the advantage in the 21st minute, capitalizing on a defensive lapse to put Chicago in a commanding position early on. Faced with a mountain to climb, New York City FC displayed remarkable resilience. The comeback began in the 29th minute when Agustin Ojeda finished off a brilliant pass from Andres Perea . The momentum had swung, and just before the interval, the provider turned scorer as Ojeda set up Malachi Jones for the equalizer in the 41st minute. In just over half an hour, the game had been completely transformed, leaving the fans breathless as the teams headed to the locker rooms. Tactical Gridlock and Substitutions The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to find a decisive edge. Chicago introduced the legendary Robert Lewandowski at the break to spearhead their attack, while New York City FC brought on fresh legs like Mitja Ilenic and Benie Traore . As the stakes rose, the game became increasingly physical, resulting in a flurry of yellow cards for Dje D'Avilla , Nicolas Fernandez , and Joel Waterman . Despite the attacking talent on display, including late cameos from Hannes Wolf and Arnau Farnos , neither side could find a late winner. The defensive units stepped up their intensity in the closing stages, ensuring that the spoils were shared. When the final whistle blew after seven minutes of stoppage time, it brought an end to an exhilarating contest that showcased the very best of North American football."
